@meta
id: 12-07
title: Drill — star, then keep going
chapter: 12
type: drill
skills: search-star, search-next
par: 28
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: double-click, Ctrl+F, Enter, Enter, Enter, Enter
open: invoice.status.ts

@brief
Eight times: `VOID` appears six times in this file. Change the last one —
the one in `reopenableStatuses` — to `CANCELLED`. Leave the other five.

Start from the `VOID` on line 1 and let the search do the walking.

@keys
| `*` | search for the word under the cursor |
| `n` | the next match of it |
| `ciw` | change the word the cursor is on |

@hints
Put the cursor on the first `VOID`, press the key that searches for the
word under it, then step to the last match.
--
`fV` gets you onto the word. `*` takes you to the second occurrence —
`*` moves as well as searching — so it is `*` and then four `n`s.

@solution
fV  *  n n n n  ciwCANCELLED<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

The rhythm is what you are drilling: land on a word, `*`, then `n` `n`
`n` until the cursor is where you want it. No scrolling, no counting
lines, no reading the file between jumps — you can see where you are from
the highlight.

Remember that `*` itself moves you to the *next* match, not the one you
are standing on. That off-by-one trips people up when they count
occurrences: from the first, `*` plus four `n` lands on the sixth.

@start invoice.status.ts
export type InvoiceStatus = 'DRAFT' | 'ISSUED' | 'PAID' | 'VOID';

export const invoiceTransitions: Record<InvoiceStatus, InvoiceStatus[]> = {
  DRAFT: ['ISSUED', 'VOID'],
  ISSUED: ['PAID', 'VOID'],
  PAID: [],
  VOID: [],
};

export const invoiceLabels: Record<InvoiceStatus, string> = {
  DRAFT: 'Draft',
  ISSUED: 'Issued',
  PAID: 'Paid',
  VOID: 'Voided',
};

export const editableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['DRAFT'];

export const payableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['ISSUED'];

export const reopenableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['VOID'];

@expected invoice.status.ts
export type InvoiceStatus = 'DRAFT' | 'ISSUED' | 'PAID' | 'VOID';

export const invoiceTransitions: Record<InvoiceStatus, InvoiceStatus[]> = {
  DRAFT: ['ISSUED', 'VOID'],
  ISSUED: ['PAID', 'VOID'],
  PAID: [],
  VOID: [],
};

export const invoiceLabels: Record<InvoiceStatus, string> = {
  DRAFT: 'Draft',
  ISSUED: 'Issued',
  PAID: 'Paid',
  VOID: 'Voided',
};

export const editableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['DRAFT'];

export const payableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['ISSUED'];

export const reopenableStatuses: InvoiceStatus[] = ['CANCELLED'];
